WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.055
Now the core operation. For every token we compute three vectors: a query, a key and a value, by multiplying the embedding with W Q, W K and W V.

00:00:08.455 --> 00:00:12.844
The score between token i and token j is the dot product of query i with key j.

00:00:13.244 --> 00:00:21.077
We divide by the square root of d k, the key dimension, so the scores do not grow with the vector length and softmax stays in a useful range.

00:00:21.477 --> 00:00:25.755
Softmax over the row turns the scores into attention weights that sum to one.

00:00:26.155 --> 00:00:30.822
The output for token i is the weighted sum of all value vectors using those weights.

00:00:31.222 --> 00:00:37.833
Multi-head attention runs this several times in parallel with smaller heads, then concatenates and projects the result.

00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:45.344
In a decoder we add a causal mask: positions after i get minus infinity before the softmax so a token cannot look at the future.
